  "id": "COMPOUND:17818 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Aesculioside B appears to exert its biological effects through a series of molecular pathways ultimately targeting the CD276 antigen. The evidence suggests that Aesculioside B acts as a target for WI-38 cells, which are then targeted by multiple compounds, including 2,5-Imino-2,5,6-Trideoxy-D-Manno-Heptitol and 3-Epidehydrotrametenolic Acid. These compounds, in turn, direct their targets to CD276 antigen. While the exact mechanism by which Aesculioside B influences WI-38 cells remains unclear, the shared targeting of CD276 antigen by multiple downstream molecules implies a potential role in the regulation of this antigen. The integration of these pathways suggests that Aesculioside B may modulate CD276 antigen expression or activity through a complex network of interactions, possibly involving the activation of signaling pathways that influence cell surface receptors. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Aesculioside B may function as a modulator of CD276 antigen, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular mechanism.",
